WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.112
The model does not receive raw text directly.

00:00:03.112 --> 00:00:10.367
A tokenizer breaks the text into vocabulary pieces and maps those pieces to integer I D's.

00:00:10.367 --> 00:00:20.067
Different model families can tokenize the same sentence differently, which affects token count, context usage,

00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:21.602
and sometimes cost.

00:00:21.602 --> 00:00:31.042
For example, a technical identifier such as `patient_id` might become one token in one tokenizer and several tokens in

00:00:31.042 --> 00:00:35.855
another. That difference changes how much context space the text consumes.
